# Credentials for the NEW, dedicated LegalHelp911 Supabase project.
# Copy this file to .env.newsupabase (gitignored) and fill in all three,
# then run: node scripts/switch-supabase.js
#
# When creating the project, use these settings:
#   Region                          East US (N. Virginia), matching Vercel's iad1
#   Enable Data API                 ON  (the lead API posts to /rest/v1/)
#   Automatically expose new tables OFF (leads must not be anon-readable;
#                                        the switch script revokes it anyway)
#   Enable automatic RLS            optional, the schema enables RLS itself
#
# Where to find each value in the Supabase dashboard for the new project:
#
#   NEW_SUPABASE_URL
#     Project Settings > Data API > Project URL
#
#   NEW_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
#     Project Settings > API Keys > "Secret keys" > default (reveal, copy).
#     Newer projects issue "sb_secret_..." keys; older ones issue a
#     "service_role" JWT starting "eyJ". Either works, both assume the
#     service_role Postgres role. Never the publishable/anon key.
#
#   NEW_DATABASE_URL
#     Connect > Session pooler (or Direct connection) > URI
#     Replace [YOUR-PASSWORD] with the database password you set when
#     creating the project.

NEW_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-NEW-REF.supabase.co
NEW_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
NEW_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.YOUR-NEW-REF:YOUR-PASSWORD@aws-0-us-east-1.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
